From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 08:43:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] TileLang V4.1 indexer: the score ReLU keeps a NaN

max(dot, 0) lowers to fmaxf and turns a NaN head dot (an infinite query or
key quantizes to the UE8M0 scale 0xFF) into zero, so the head silently
contributed nothing. DeepSeek's indexer uses relu_, which keeps the NaN.
Pass a NaN through and keep max for everything else, so every other value,
signed zeros included, has the same bits as before. The generated code
evaluates the two values of each pair in a short loop instead of one
float2 max.
---
 vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/indexer.py | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/indexer.py b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/indexer.py
index d12b37e8c..a08b330e2 100644
--- a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/indexer.py
+++ b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/indexer.py
@@ -170,8 +170,11 @@ def indexer_score_v41(
                 sf_b_granularity_k=SF_BLOCK,
             )
             # The published rounding stages: BF16 dot, ReLU, BF16 weighted product.
+            # The ReLU keeps a NaN, as the reference's relu_ does; max alone would
+            # drop it. Every other value, signed zeros included, takes max's bits.
             for p, h in T.Parallel(block_P, heads):
-                dot = T.max(T.cast(T.cast(acc[p, h], T.bfloat16), accum_dtype), 0.0)
+                dot = T.cast(T.cast(acc[p, h], T.bfloat16), accum_dtype)
+                dot = T.if_then_else(T.isnan(dot), dot, T.max(dot, 0.0))
                 contrib[p, h] = T.cast(
                     T.cast(T.fmul(dot, W_shared[h]), T.bfloat16), accum_dtype
                 )
